<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Larger Grids</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ C.2 Larger Grids ‣ Appendix C Additional Simulation Results ‣ Foundation Models as World Models: A Foundational Study in Text-Based GridWorlds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows the simulation accuracy for the GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 models with grid sizes <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[5,8,16]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[5,8,16]</annotation></semantics></math>. Figure <a href="#A3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ C.2 Larger Grids ‣ Appendix C Additional Simulation Results ‣ Foundation Models as World Models: A Foundational Study in Text-Based GridWorlds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows the errors made by the models. As can be observed, the models remain consistent in terms of accuracy despite the grid size increases.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T3.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A3.T3.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Simulation accuracy results for the GPT models with varying grid sizes. Prompt <math id="A3.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> queries the transition function with detailed descriptions, <math id="A3.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T+R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T+R</annotation></semantics></math> queries both the transition and reward function with detailed descriptions, and prompt <math id="A3.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{minimal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>minimal</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{minimal}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{minimal}}+R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>minimal</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{minimal}}+R</annotation></semantics></math> the former prompts with minimal transition function descriptions.</span></figcaption>
